A||N||4||fropuff||How should I do this???||||1||
Z||000000||fropuff||11-18-2000||01:49 PM||||Hey, I just got back from the salvage yard from getting an AM/FM for my Cutlass.  I got one, and it works, but I can't get any reception.  I can't get any FM stations; just one AM, Radio Disney!  Not something I would listen to.  I need to get some kind of an antenna.  What would work good?  Thanks.<P>PS:  There were SEVEN Fieros there!  All 4-cyl notchbacks, though.  They were all kids cars.  Coincidence?  I think not.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||deceler8||11-18-2000||03:22 PM||||Unless your Cutlass didn't have a radio from the factory, there should be an antenna (they're embedded in the windshield glass).<P>Look around behind the radio opening...it may be there unless someone removed it.<P>If it ain't there, about any aftermarket antenna will do the trick. They even sell one that attaches to the windshield (tape with wire attached to it) just like from the factory.||||reg||1
Z||000002||deceler8||11-18-2000||03:25 PM||||Also, as I recall, the old Delco radios have a "trimmer" that you can adjust to aid reception. It's a little slot with a screwdriver hole that you turn (it should be on the front of the radio) to adjust reception. I believe you tune to an AM station around 1600 (or whatever you can pick up) and turn the screwq until it comes in loudest.||||reg||1
Z||000003||fropuff||11-18-2000||08:11 PM||||Yeah, I've got the windshield antenna.  I will try the trimmer thing first, then I might get a mast antenna kit from Radio Shack.  Thanks for the help.  <P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fropuff||11-20-2000||06:22 PM||||Well, I tried the screw adjuster.  It didn't change a thing.  I can't even get an AM station any more.  Do you think I should get an antenna kit tomorrow from Radio Shack?  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Fuzz busters are for those who are worried about being caught.||||reg||1
